  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 255 PM Thursday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... After continued below average temperatures and \nhumidity levels to finish this work week, moisture and probability \nof convection will increase by late weekend and continue into early \nto mid next week. \n\nThe models indicate a positively-tilted mid/upr-level trough will \nprogress slowly ewd from ern Canada through the OH and TN Valleys \nthis weekend through early next week, though there remains \nsignificant model spread regarding to what degree the trough will \nremain phased, and similarly to what degree and duration the basal \nportion may close off across the TN Valley vicinity next week. In \nany event, deep sswly flow will transport abundant moisture, \ncharacterized by PWs of around 2.25\" and 125% or so of normal, \nacross the Carolinas and srn Middle Atlantic Sun through at least \nMon night, when clouds and precipitation chances in convection will \nbe maximized. If deeper trough and closed low solutions were to \nverify, some severe risk would exist for cntl NC during that time.\n\nWhile the trough and whatever closed low that may form over the TN \nValley should continue to lift newd and deamplify by mid to late \nnext week, residually moist, swly flow and chances for rain will \nprobably persist over cntl NC for most of the forecast period.",
